				<div class="et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_13 mini-head et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h2>Installation Tips That Actually Matter</h2>
<ul>
<li>Hire a certified HVAC expert — this isn’t a DIY job; proper setup keeps the system safe and running smoothly.</li>
<li>Check your ductwork first — leaky ducts waste heat and undercut even the best new furnace.<br />
Size it right, not big — an oversized furnace cycles on and off more, wearing out faster instead of heating better.</li>
<li>Ask for a safety check — vents and gas lines should be confirmed sealed before the system is fired up.<br />
Keep the manual handy — you’ll want it for filter schedules, warranty terms, and seasonal maintenance.</li>
</ul></div>
			</div>
