				<div class="et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_14 mini-head et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h2>Preventing Costly Heating Repairs</h2>
<p>Regular maintenance catches small issues before they become expensive ones, and keeps manufacturer warranties valid. Between professional visits:</p>
<ul>
<li>Change filters every 1–2 months during heating season</li>
<li>Don’t block air vents with furniture or curtains<br />
Book a yearly service check before winter starts</li>
<li>Listen for new sounds — humming, knocking, or rattling are early warning signs</li>
<li>Keep the area around the furnace clean and clear</li>
</ul>
<p>We recommend professional heating maintenance annually, before heating season, to prevent breakdowns, maintain efficiency, extend system life, and ensure safe operation.</p></div>
